(c) the number of tickets for non-AC sleeper coaches sold across the country and total revenue earned by Railways during the years 2021-22, 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 and 2025-26?

(a) the length and cost of the Purvanchal Expressway and the Gorakhpur Purvanchal Link Expressway;
(b) the area of land acquired and the number of farmers from whom the land was acquired for the construction of said Expressways; and
(c) the volume of trucks, buses, other four-wheelers and two-wheelers using both expressways during the years 2024-25 and 2025-26 and the amount of the revenue generated?

(a) the manner in which utilisation of 10 per cent gross budgetary support by other Central Ministries is being monitored to ensure the dedicated investment target of ?1.14 lakh crore for the North Eastern Region (NER);
(b) the expected impact of increase in the share of taxes for the region on the financial autonomy of smaller States;
(c) whether one hundred per cent real-time monitoring of all central projects in the region has been ensured through the Poorvottar Vikas Setu Portal by February 2026; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the rules governing the leasing or sale of land to citizens or private entities by the Rail Land Development Authority (RLDA);
(b) the basis on which the lease/sale value is assessed, the nature of development required to be undertaken by the land developer, and the revenue that accrues to Railways therefrom; and
(c) the details of the total land measured in Gorakhpur during the last five years, including the transaction price of the area leased or sold, and the corresponding circle and market rates prevailing at that time?

(a) whether it is a fact that about 400 families in New Indira Colony (slum) of Sector-13, Chandigarh have been living on the land belonging to Municipal Corporation for the last 40 years and they have all the proof like ration cards, electricity connections, aadhaar cards and voter cards;
(b) whether the Chandigarh Administration/Municipal Corporation would provide them the benefit of private housing by getting them covered under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (urban) or any other scheme; and
(c) if so, by when?

(a) the  number of  beneficiaries of Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY), Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana, Surakshit Matritva Abhiyan, Health and Wellness Center and Janani Suraksha Yojana in the State of Kerala, district-wise;
(b) whether Government of Kerala made any changes in the nature of AB-PMJAY;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) the difficulties faced in implementing all schemes, including AB-PMJAY as a result of these changes; and
(e)  the positive results in all the health statistics of Kerala with the efforts of Government since 2018?

(a) the Minimum Support Price (MSP) announced for paddy producing farmers of Kerala by the Central Government and whether Government of Kerala has announced any bonus in addition to the MSP;
(b) the quantum and price at which paddy was purchased in Kerala during the years 2019-20, 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23; and
(c) the amount paid separately under the heads of MSP and special bonus by Government of Kerala along with the amount yet to be paid and by when the same will be fully paid?

(a) the number of women working in newspapers and channels of Government as well as private sector during the years 2019-20 to 2022-2023 in various States of the country;
(b) whether any special provisions have been made for the improvement, safety, professional development, gender equality and prevention of exploitation of these women journalists under Government policies; and
(c) whether Government has conducted any study regarding the above challenges being faced by women journalists, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the changes that have been made by Government of Kerala in the implementation of Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) and whether house built under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana is written on such constructed houses or not;
(b) the number of separate houses which have been constructed in different assembly constituencies of Kerala; and
(c) whether Government will consider checking the eligibility of the allotted houses?

(a) the eligibility criteria fixed for PM-Kisan Samman Nidhi Yojana (PM-KISAN) and the number of farmers and beneficiaries in different States of the country;
(b)  the number of beneficiaries in proportion to the number of farmers, in different assembly constituencies of Kerala; and
(c)  the reasons as to why some farmers of Kerala have not received the last 2-3 instalments of PM-KISAN and whether Government will investigate the matter?

(a) the details of the employer and Government contribution, the income received from  interest and fund credited every year in invested income and corpus fund at the end of the year along with number of pensioners under the Employees' Pension Scheme, 1995 during the years 2019-20, 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23;
(b) the amount paid as pension to the retired personnel and various types of dependents every year under the scheme during the above period; and 
(c) the additional amount of funds required in case the minimum pension of ? 1000 would be increased to ? 5000, ? 6000 or ? 7000?

(a) the details of the achievements made with regard to the scheme PMAY-G in different States of the country in proportion to their population;
(b) whether Government of Kerala has made any changes in the nature of the scheme, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether the sentence "Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana se Nirmit Awaas" has been displayed on the houses constructed under the scheme; and
(d) the details of the achievements made with regard to the scheme in different constituencies of Kerala?

