(a) whether the villages namely Neelamperur, Veliyanad, Kavalam, Kainakary, Pulinkunnu, Ramankari, Talwadi etc. in Kuttanad region of Kerala are witnessing an increase in cancer patients during the last twenty five years;
(b) if so, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the details of the kind of researches undertaken and action taken to control it?

(a) whether the Archaeological Survey of India, while mentioning King Ugrasen as the ancestor of the Agrawal community, has described Agrasen's stepwell as Ugrasen's stepwell in the rock inscription displayed at the main gate of Agrasen's stepwell located at Hailey Road, Delhi; 
(b) whether Government would conduct a high-level inquiry into this foul play with the glorious history of the Agrawal community, and give directions to punish the culprits and to change the inscriptions and name plates of the site; and
(c) if so, by when, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of Amrit Sarovars identified  under Mission Amrit Sarovar of MGNREGA scheme in various States of the country;
(b) the number of Amrit Sarovars out of the above where work has been started/completed;
(c) the average capacity of the Amrit Sarovars constructed in each State and the average per capita water conserved through them; and 
(d) the details of Amrit Sarovars constructed in Gorakhpur district of Uttar Pradesh?

(a) whether the review panel constituted by National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC) headed by Shri J P Singh Joorel, Director, Information and Library Network (INFLIBNET), has submitted any of its reports to the UGC on 26th September, 2022 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether UGC has taken any action on that report and if so, the details thereof, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government would take cognizance of the report and consider it?

(a) the achievement against various goals, targets, and national indicators on Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) in different States of the country;
(b) the reasons responsible for certain States remaining under the category of 'aspirant States till date and the reasons therefor; and
(c) the action being taken by Government for better performance thereof?

(a) the details of crop loans received by various States of the country and their gross value output during the last three years;
(b) whether the credit received by some States is much higher than their gross agricultural output; and 
(c) whether Government has conducted any inquiry in this regard, if so, the Report thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether any Central Sector Scheme under "Prime Minister's Development Initiative for North East Region" was announced in the budget for the year 2022-23 and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has included any plan in the Scheme keeping in view the vast natural potential of the region; and
(c) if so, the works  approved, started, completed under the said Scheme along with their cost, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) whether a commitment to ensure adequate number of teachers in subjects like arts, physical education, vocational education and language has been made in point 5.5 of the New Education Policy (NEP)-2020;
(b) if so, whether Government has put in place any guiding principle, policy and rules in this direction and whether any action plan for creation of permanent posts has been chalked out to implement the commitment on the ground so far; and
(c) whether Government would consider giving preference to experienced instructors of these subjects while appointing them to these posts?

(a) the recommendations made by the Thirteenth, Fourteenth and Fifteenth Finance Commissions respectively with regard to the establishment of an independent Fiscal Council in the country;
(b) the benefits enumerated by the Finance Commissions with regard to the financial management of the country on account of establishment of this Council; and
(c) the reasons due to which Government has not taken any action for its implementation despite repeated recommendations?

(a) the number of micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) running in various States across the country during the years 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-2023, along with the details of capital invested therein and employment generated thereby;
(b) the number of industries out of these running in profits and those remaining closed, State-wise details thereof; and
(c) the action being taken by Government to revive these closed down industries?

(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that a number of social media companies, especially Facebook/ Meta are found to be deliberately uploading immoral and sexually provocative contents along with the tool kits to hurt profoundly the Indian family system and sanctity of relations; 
(b) whether Government has taken any steps to proscribe the same; and
(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number and details of unskilled and skilled migrated labourers from other States in organized and unorganized sector in different States of the country during the years 2020-21, 2021-22 and 2022-23, the number of labourers who came back in 2020-21 and went back in 2021-22 and 2022-23;
(b) whether Government has made any arrangement for necessary registration of workers going to other States; 
(c) if so, the State-wise number of registered organized/unorganized and skilled/unskilled workers; and
(d) whether Government would consider setting up of any regulatory commission for 100 per cent registration of workers?

